 might be failing due to a missing dependency or a configuration error. Similarly, the 'user' pod might have issues with its container. \n\nSo, the next logical step is to check the logs of the 'rate-6fff88f6f5-6mxgg' pod. The command would be 'kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-6mxgg -n hotel-reservation'. That should retrieve the logs for that specific pod, which might indicate why it's restarting. If that doesn't show anything, then check the 'user' pod's logs next. But since each tool call is a single command, the user should start with one pod first. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the user should check the logs for the 'geo' pod since there was a 'BackOff restarting failed container' event. But the 'geo' pod's status is 'Running' with 2 restarts. So checking its logs could also be useful. However, the user's focus is on the pods with restarts mentioned in the previous steps. \n\nIn any case, the correct approach is to use 'kubectl logs' on the specific pods that have restarts. The user needs to pick one pod to check first. Let's go with 'rate-6fff88f6f5-6mxgg' as it has two restarts, which might indicate a more persistent issue.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-6mxgg -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-882b008ce08384b4', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 699, 'prompt_tokens': 8257, 'total_tokens': 8956, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc1c-e110-7352-99ad-2799df1840b7-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-6mxgg -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-882b008ce08384b4', 'type': 'tool_call'}], 