hy it's restarting. If that doesn't show anything, then check the 'user' pod's logs next. But since each tool call is a single command, the user should start with one pod first. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the user should check the logs for the 'geo' pod since there was a 'BackOff restarting failed container' event. But the 'geo' pod's status is 'Running' with 2 restarts. So checking its logs could also be useful. However, the user's focus is on the pods with restarts mentioned in the previous steps. \n\nIn any case, the correct approach is to use 'kubectl logs' on the specific pods that have restarts. The user needs to pick one pod to check first. Let's go with 'rate-6fff88f6f5-6mxgg' as it has two restarts, which might indicate a more persistent issue.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-6mxgg -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-882b008ce08384b4', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 699, 'prompt_tokens': 8257, 'total_tokens': 8956, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc1c-e110-7352-99ad-2799df1840b7-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-6mxgg -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-882b008ce08384b4', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 8257, 'output_tokens': 699, 'total_tokens': 8956}), ToolMessage(content='{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T14:03:12Z","message":"TLS disabled."}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T14:03:12Z","message":"Set global log level: info"}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T14:03:12Z","message":"Tune: setGCPercent to 100"}\n\x1