e did. The error might be due to the answer format. The previous submission had a nested structure, but maybe the system expects a flat dictionary. \n\nSo, the user should try submitting an empty dict again, as the initial example did, to bypass the stage issue. That might be the only way to proceed since the system is in teardown and not allowing submissions.\n</think>\n\ntool name: submit_tool\n\nJustification: The system is still in the 'tearing_down' stage, which prevents submissions. To comply with the system's constraints, the final answer must be submitted as an empty dictionary to bypass the stage restriction while confirming the fault resolution. \n\nNext, generate the tool call for `submit_tool` with an empty dict.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 585, 'prompt_tokens': 6886, 'total_tokens': 7471, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc21-f9ca-7802-8acc-4c58c362a575-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6886, 'output_tokens': 585, 'total_tokens': 7471}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='845f4276-b28d-43d5-baa2-6c41d78378b7'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to submit a solution for an IT incident involving a Kubernetes cluster. The main issue was a pod named \'rate\' that kept restarting with exit code 2. The LLM went through a series of steps to diagnose and fix the problem.\n\nFirst, they checked the pod\'s YAML configuration and noticed the command was set to ["rate"], which might not be correct. Then, they tried to get the pod\'s logs but got a "Not Found" error, which made them check 